#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW Human review"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Low-confidence results go to people, whose decisions are leased, durable and never overwritten by machines."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: product · depends on: [CAP-OPERATIONALDB]{1}, [CAP-AUDIT]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Route uncertain results to people and keep their decisions safe from machines and from each other."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A low-confidence guess is worse than no answer ([P10]{1}). Mutual exclusion belongs in the database, where one statement can claim an item."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A review queue; leases as database keys; typed attribution of decisions."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A result below its confidence threshold is routed to review with a reason code; thresholds live in one configuration module."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Grep finds thresholds only in the configuration module; a low-confidence fixture lands in review."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A reviewer claims an item with a lease held as a database key; claim is one statement, expiry is judged at read time, and a commit requires a live lease checked before its first write.{1}*Example:* Two reviewers open the same item; the first claim inserts the lease, and the second finds a live lease and is refused."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A race test with concurrent sessions yields exactly one holder."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "A human decision outranks any machine re-delivery or re-run; guards test the condition that would make a write wrong, not a status label."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Re-run the pipeline over a reviewed item; the human decision is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Decisions are reversed by a compensating action that keeps both records; nothing is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Undo a decision; both the decision and its reversal are present."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "CAP-REVIEW.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Each decision records its kind of attribution (automatic, affirmed, corrected, backfilled) so reporting can tell who or what decided."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-review.md
msgid "Reporting groups decisions by attribution."
msgstr ""

